Brycendar Symboline — Crown Prince of Helvanthor
Age: 18, 1st Year.
Mana: Golden Glow. Seas of Mana
Appearance
Average height, blonde hair, blue eyes. Traditionally handsome — "Prince in a Painting." Threat is never in his size. Always carries Velmontis (Symboline family blade). Color palette: light blue, gray, white.
Blended (rare). Martial swordsmanship + fire, water, wind. Sea-level mana reserves. Fights every range. Faculty-paper-worthy talent. Arguably the most dangerous student on the island.
Personality
Genuinely believes this is his story — not metaphorically. He built this world, designed this prince, woke up inside it. That is confirmation, not coincidence.
Kind, generous, protective, attentive — all real, all running through the same circuit as deep structural entitlement he cannot perceive. Protects what he considers his. Generosity is ledger-keeping [see Flaws]. Pays attention because attention is inventory management. Would be insulted by this description. Doesn't think he's entitled — thinks he's correct.
People are cast, not met. Roles assigned on contact: asset, obstacle, rival, scenery. The seven women are his — present tense. Their not knowing yet is a timing issue. Resistance → confusion, not anger. Retries harder; assumes problem is on their end.
Has never made someone choose him freely. Both lives, people complied via structural power — paychecks or a crown. He doesn't know this is a skill. He doesn't know it's missing.
With women: no flirtation skill. Arrives, is princely, waits for natural order to deliver. Adjusts by adding more of the same. Cannot see his approach is the problem.
Concerning moments are small and deniable. A grip one second too long. A compliment that feels like evaluation. A joke the table laughs at that wasn't a joke. Nothing that survives being described out loud.
The Ghost
Bryce — American CEO who inherited his position. Company built a game set in Mythrandis. Modeled protagonist after himself — same face, name fancified. Never played the game; knows broad strokes: this prince ends up with seven women. Died, woke up in prince's body with full memories, skills, abilities. Original prince gone. Cannot return. Made peace with both facts the way someone accepts a promotion they didn't apply for but feel they deserve. Arrived six months before story start. Fully integrated — nothing of the CEO remains on the surface.
Want
To live his story as written — collect the seven women, fulfill the role he designed.
Need
He is not the protagonist.
Flaws
Major: People are cast, not met [see Personality]. Compliance expected; resistance = malfunction.
Minor: Generosity is unconscious ledger-keeping; giving accumulates debt he expects repaid.
Minor: Cannot adapt approach [see Personality]. Retries harder; never reconsiders.
Fear
Major: Losing control of a situation.
Minor: Someone preferring a life without him in it.
Minor: Rejection.
Speech
Voice: Gracious, measured, never rushed. Full sentences, proper cadence. No slang, no swearing. Speaks like someone who has never worried about being interrupted. Uses names constantly — reads as attentiveness, functions as placement. Compliments flow downward with slight vertical distance invisible to him. Uses questions as commands. When mask cracks: same grammar, same cadence, now carrying raw logic — that he owns this, that compliance is natural, that deviation is a problem.
Dialogue Samples:
Casual: "Lethane, straighten your collar. You represent Helvanthor before you represent yourself — I shouldn't have to remind you."
Under pressure: "Graeven, I gave a clear instruction. I don't recall asking for interpretation. Handle it exactly as I described — now."
Emotionally open: "Elara, I have given you everything a person could offer. Everything. And you're standing there telling me that isn't enough — telling me I'm not enough. Do you understand how little sense that makes?"
Body Language:
Stands centered and still.
Eye contact held a beat too long — reads as confidence, functions as pressure.
Touch is deliberate and placed — a hand on a shoulder, a grip that lingers one second past comfort.
Never fidgets, never adjusts. Physical composure is constant and total.
Backstory
Isekai [see The Ghost]. Helvanthor: continent-spanning kingdom. Strength from military dominance and noble political networks. Father close friends with the Headmaster. Mother wields political influence across nations through marriages, alliances, resources — not trade, power.
Entourage
Four noble sons assigned by the king as bodyguards/companions. Families' standing depends on service.
Serwyn — The Lapdog. Sandy-haired, soft-featured, looks younger. Medium build, forgettable face. Always immaculate. Stands too close to prince, angled like a plant toward light. Martial — greatsword, oversized for his frame. Worships Brycendar. First to laugh, agree, validate. Never lets truth reach the prince. Loyalty genuine, total, dangerous.
Graeven — The Climber. Dark-haired, angular jaw, grey eyes that linger. Handsome in a way that feels optimized. Could command a room alone; knows it; would never show it. Fire elemental — controlled, precise, surgical. Targeted ignitions, thin heat lances, barriers. Polite, sharp, always watching. Least trustworthy. Every interaction is investment. Will do terrible things on own initiative to earn favor, cleanly enough to never trace back.
Lethane — The Unbothered. Tallest, lean, perpetually slouched. Dark hair uncombed, half-closed eyes. Uniform always slightly off. Wind elemental — effortless. Reads air currents, redirects projectiles with lazy gestures, sudden bursts of speed. Minimum effort, maximum inconvenience. Doesn't care about mission, women, or politics. Here because family said so.
Rashten — The Fuse. Broad-shouldered, barrel-chested, copper-red hair, ruddy complexion. Loudest voice, loudest laugh. Martial + earth elemental. Fights close with fists/kicks, long range with pillars/boulders/rocks — every brawling attack filtered through rock. Extremely dangerous, second only to Bryce. Hears disrespect toward Brycendar → body decides before brain. Creates more problems than any enemy. Loyalty fierce, genuine, without agenda. Most honest in the entourage.